[12.015196, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[12.049974, "o", "[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-01 (14.2) the runtimeSessionId comes from the browser: AgentCore does not enforce session-to-user mappings, so a replayed ID lands in someone else's microVM\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-02 (14.2) tsg-web-frontend (end-user reachable) may call InvokeAgentRuntime, InvokeAgentRuntimeCommand, InvokeAgentRuntimeCommandShell on the runtime: InvokeAgentRuntimeCommand runs shell commands in a session without the model\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-03 (14.2) the entrypoint passes the payload's prompt to the framework without checking it is a string: a toolUse block runs a tool with no model in the loop (AgentCore Runtime has no server-side protection for this)\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-04 (14.2) the execution role has 10 grants on wildcards (*, memory/*, runtime/*): one compromised session can read other agents' memory, call other runtimes and sandboxes (Unit 42 'Agent God Mode')\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-06 (14.3) SigV4 runtime and the backend copies runtimeUserId from the browser: AgentCore treats it as an opaque string, so anyone can fetch anyone's tokens from the vault\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-07 (14.3) the gateway JWT authorizer checks only allowedScopes: a token issued to ANY app of this identity provider (a partner portal in the same user pool) is accepted\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-12 (14.4) tsg-web-frontend may invoke the tools Lambda directly: that path skips the gateway's authorizer and policy engine\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-13 (14.4) the agent calls the gateway with its own client-credentials token: every tool call looks like the agent, so the gateway policy can't tell Bob from Alice\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-16 (14.5) the policy engine is attached in LOG_ONLY mode: every tool call succeeds regardless of forbid policies\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-17 (14.5) the Cedar policies ALLOW: Bob resets the CEO's MFA naming the CEO as caller\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-18 (14.5) tsg-web-frontend may call UpdateGateway: that permission alone can set the mode to LOG_ONLY or remove the policy engine\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-21 (14.6) long-term memory namespace /helpdesk/facts/ has no {actorId}: what one user teaches the agent, every user gets back\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-22 (14.6) the agent takes the memory actorId from the request: a user can read or write another user's memories\r\n[\u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K  ] M14-24 (14.6) a Code Interpreter (PUBLIC network, with an execution role) the task does not need: even SANDBOX mode can reach Amazon S3 and resolve DNS\r\n14 \u001b[01;31m\u001b[KHIGH\u001b[m\u001b[K, 11 MEDIUM, 2 LOW  (27 findings)\r\n"]
